    "description": "- Unlocked $70+ million in value by architecting and developing a full-stack, GenAI-powered content validation system; designed the responsive frontend with Vue and TypeScript, while building the backend service using Python, FastAPI, LangGraph, and Ollama 3.1 70B LLM on Kubernetes to automatically validate marketing content against legal requirements, dramatically reducing legal review cycle times.\n- Played a pivotal role in a collaborative team effort to develop an email marketing pipeline, utilizing Python and AWS services (Lambda, SQS) for targeted outreach to 8 million Capital One customers. This initiative eliminated dependency on Salesforce Marketing Cloud, contributing to $5 million in annual savings.\n- Enhanced critical e-filing components using AWS Step Functions and Lambda, contributing to a 20% reduction in filing errors for Capital One's Cash Transaction reports (CTRs) to FINCEN, resulting in approximately $2 million in annual savings.\n- Implemented serverless architecture using AWS Lambda functions, Aurora Databases, S3 buckets, and Step Functions, reducing infrastructure costs by 30%, saving roughly $10,000 monthly.\n- Led failover activities for all e-filing components across AWS regions, ensuring application resilience and uninterrupted filing of cash transaction reports. This effort potentially saved Capital One Risk Management teams around $25,000 per potential region outage.",
